  "text": "Classic Neapolitan ice cream is a traditional Italian dessert that combines three distinct flavors: vanilla, chocolate, and strawberry. It\u2019s a beloved treat, especially in Naples, and is often enjoyed in small, individual portions. Here\u2019s a simple and authentic recipe to make your own Neapolitan ice cream at home:\n\n---\n\n### **Classic Neapolitan Ice Cream Recipe**\n\n#### **Ingredients** (for 4 servings):\n- 2 cups (400g) heavy cream  \n- 1 cup (240ml) whole milk  \n- 3/4 cup (60g) sugar  \n- 1/2 tsp vanilla extract  \n- 1/2 cup (60g) chocolate chips or melted chocolate  \n- 1/2 cup (80g) strawberries, mashed (about 4 medium strawberries)  \n- 1/4 tsp salt  \n\n---\n\n#### **Instructions**:\n\n1. **Combine the base**:\n   - In a large mixing bowl, combine the heavy cream, whole milk, sugar, vanilla extract, and salt.  \n   - Whisk until the sugar is fully dissolved and the mixture is smooth.\n\n2. **Chill the mixture**:\n   - Cover the bowl and refrigerate for at least 2 hours or until completely cold. This helps the ice cream churn more smoothly.\n\n3. **Churn the ice cream**:\n   - Pour the chilled mixture into an ice cream maker. Churn according to the manufacturer\u2019s instructions, usually 20\u201325 minutes, until it reaches a soft-serve consistency.\n\n4. **Divide and add flavors**:\n   - Once the base is ready, divide the mixture into three equal parts in separate bowls or containers.\n\n5. **Add the flavors**:\n   - **Vanilla**: Leave one portion as-is or stir in a pinch of salt for a subtle contrast.\n   - **Chocolate**: Melt some good quality chocolate (dark or semi-sweet) and stir it into the second portion. You can also swirl in some chocolate chips for texture.\n   - **Strawberry**: Mash the strawberries and strain to remove seeds. Add the mashed strawberries to the third portion and mix well.\n\n6. **Freeze**:\n   - Transfer each flavor to airtight containers and freeze for at least 2\u20133 hours, or until firm.\n\n7. **Serve**:\n   - Let the ice cream sit at room temperature for a few minutes before serving for the best texture. Serve in small scoops, just like the original Neapolitan style.\n\n---\n\n### **Tips for Authenticity**:\n- Use high-quality chocolate for a rich, authentic flavor.\n- For a softer texture, use a bit of egg yolk in your base (optional), but this is not traditional.\n- Neapolitan ice cream is typically served in small cones or cups, often with a sprinkling of chocolate shavings or a cherry on top.\n\nEnjoy your homemade Neapolitan ice cream! \ud83c\udf66",
